#. translators: Heading of the notice shown on the WordPress dashboard and
#. plugins screen after WPML stopped adding hreflang tags to the page head.
#. "Hreflang" is an HTML attribute name and stays in English.
#: classes/Shared/HeadLangsNoticeHooks.php:79
msgid "Hreflang tags moved to your sitemap"
msgstr "A hreflang címkék átkerültek a webhelytérképre"

#. translators: Text of the "Hreflang tags moved to your sitemap" notice.
#. "<head>" is the name of an HTML section and must stay exactly as it is.
#: classes/Shared/HeadLangsNoticeHooks.php:80
msgid ""
"To improve SEO and avoid duplicate hreflang data, WPML now adds hreflang "
"tags only to your sitemap. We have disabled the hreflang tags in your page's"
" <head> section."
msgstr "Az SEO javítása és a duplikált hreflang adatok elkerülése érdekében a WPML mostantól csak a webhelytérképre adja hozzá a hreflang címkéket. Letiltottuk az oldalad <head> szakaszában lévő hreflang címkéket."

#. translators: Last line of the "Hreflang tags moved to your sitemap" notice.
#. %1$s: opening link tag, %2$s: closing link tag. The words between them are
#. a path through the WordPress admin and should read as those screens are
#. named in this language. "<head>" is the name of an HTML section and stays
#. as it is.
#: classes/Shared/HeadLangsNoticeHooks.php:84
#, php-format
msgid ""
"If you prefer to keep them in the <head>, you can re-enable this option in "
"%1$sWPML → Settings → URLs and SEO%2$s."
msgstr "Ha inkább a <head> részben szeretnéd megtartani őket, újra bekapcsolhatod ezt a beállítást itt: %1$sWPML → Settings → URLs and SEO%2$s."

#. translators: Heading of the box on the Yoast SEO settings screen that lists
#. one sitemap per language. A noun phrase, not an instruction.
#: classes/YoastSEO/Sitemap/PerLanguageSitemapsNotice.php:167
msgid "Sitemaps for each language"
msgstr "Webhelytérképek nyelvenként"

#. translators: Text inside the "Sitemaps for each language" box on the Yoast
#. SEO settings screen, above the list of addresses. "Google Search Console"
#. is a product name and stays in English.
#: classes/YoastSEO/Sitemap/PerLanguageSitemapsNotice.php:171
msgid ""
"Each language runs on its own domain, so each one has its own sitemap. "
"Submit all of them to Google Search Console."
msgstr "Minden nyelv saját domainen fut, ezért mindegyikhez külön oldaltérkép tartozik. Küldd be mindegyiket a Google Search Console-ba."

#. translators: Label shown on a Yoast SEO field on the term editing screen
#. when WPML supplies the translation and the field is read-only.
#: classes/YoastSEO/Terms/Meta/AdminScreenHooks.php:149
msgid "Translated by WPML"
msgstr "A WPML fordította"

#. translators: Explanation under that label. "Edit anyway" is the button
#. below it, so translate the two the same way. "WPML String Translation" is a
#. product name and stays in English.
#: classes/YoastSEO/Terms/Meta/AdminScreenHooks.php:150
msgid ""
"This field shows the translation that WPML String Translation serves. Click "
"\"Edit anyway\" to override it."
msgstr "Ez a mező a WPML String Translation által megjelenített fordítást mutatja. A felülbíráláshoz kattints a „Szerkesztés mindenképp” gombra."

#. translators: Button beside a read-only Yoast SEO field on the term editing
#. screen; it unlocks the field for typing. Verb, imperative. The explanation
#. above quotes it, so translate the two the same way.
#: classes/YoastSEO/Terms/Meta/AdminScreenHooks.php:151
msgid "Edit anyway"
msgstr "Szerkesztés mindenképpen"

#. translators: Explanation shown on a Yoast SEO field on the term editing
#. screen once the user has typed over WPML's translation; "it" is the field's
#. text.
#: classes/YoastSEO/Terms/Meta/AdminScreenHooks.php:152
msgid ""
"Your text overrides the WPML translation. Leave the field empty to let WPML "
"translate it."
msgstr "A szöveged felülbírálja a WPML fordítását. Hagyd üresen a mezőt, hogy a WPML lefordíthassa."

#: classes/YoastSEO/Terms/Meta/DashboardHooks.php:30
msgid ""
"This section has the Yoast SEO texts of your categories, tags and other "
"taxonomy terms."
msgstr "Ebben a szakaszban találod a kategóriáidhoz, címkéidhez és más osztályozási kifejezéseidhez tartozó Yoast SEO-szövegeket."
